    "created_at": "2016-03-02T18:26:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-02T18:26:07Z",
    "body": "I tend to think of  `¹` and `<sup>1</sup>` as semantically equivalent, and so `<sup>¹</sup>` would be semantically equivalent to `<sup><sup>1</sup></sup>`. I don't think any of these should be disallowed; there could be use cases for using both together; e.g. `<var>x<sup>y²</sup></var>`.\n\nIt seems like a good idea to add an example that discusses this. If you like you can take a stab at making a pull request for this. :-)\n",
