    "updated_at": "2016-03-02T22:10:04Z",
    "body": "+1 to what zcorpan said. Using `<sup>` on a normal digit is equivalent in meaning to using one of the special-purpose superscript digits, and this meaning is compositional.\n\nThere's no real preference to using the element vs the character.  CSS does, however, [provide a property for automatically using the char when you use the element](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts/#font-variant-position-prop)\n\nThe first example does strike me as _explicitly contradicting_ the authoring requirement in the preceding paragraph, which is amusing. ^_^\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
