    "created_at": "2016-03-03T09:18:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-03T09:18:33Z",
    "body": "I suppose the requirement should be tweaked and just say that it's OK to use for typographical conventions, even if removing the element wouldn't change the meaning (looking at Wikipedia it seems mlle and m<sup>lle</sup> are both acceptable forms).\n\nIt's not clear to me that misuse of these elements for presentational purposes has been much of a problem, so maybe it's better to not call it out and just say when these elements _are_ appropriate.\n",
